# {{name}} - GROTTE Sandbox Template

This is an GROTTE sandbox template that allows you to run code in a controlled environment.

## Prerequisites

Before you begin, make sure you have:
- An GROTTE account (sign up at [grotte.parallactic.fr](https://grotte.parallactic.fr))
- Your GROTTE API key (get it from your [GROTTE dashboard](https://grotte.parallactic.fr/dashboard))
{{#if isTypeScript}}- Node.js and npm/yarn (or similar) installed{{else if isPython}}- Python installed{{/if}}

## Configuration

1. Create a `.env` file in your project root or set the environment variable:
   ```
   GROTTE_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
   ```

## Installing Dependencies

```bash
{{#if isTypeScript}}
npm install grotte
{{else if isPython}}
pip install grotte
{{/if}}
```

## Building the Template

```bash
{{#if isTypeScript}}
# For development
npm run grotte:build:dev

# For production
npm run grotte:build:prod
{{else if isPython}}
# For development
make grotte:build:dev

# For production
make grotte:build:prod
{{/if}}
```

## Using the Template in a Sandbox

Once your template is built, you can use it in your GROTTE sandbox:

{{#if isTypeScript}}
```typescript
import { Sandbox } from 'grotte'

// Create a new sandbox instance
const sandbox = await Sandbox.create('{{name}}')

// Your sandbox is ready to use!
console.log('Sandbox created successfully')
```
{{else if isPythonSync}}
```python
from grotte import Sandbox

# Create a new sandbox instance
sandbox = Sandbox.create('{{name}}')

# Your sandbox is ready to use!
print('Sandbox created successfully')
```
{{else if isPythonAsync}}
```python
from grotte import AsyncSandbox
import asyncio

async def main():
    # Create a new sandbox instance
    sandbox = await AsyncSandbox.create('{{name}}')
    
    # Your sandbox is ready to use!
    print('Sandbox created successfully')

# Run the async function
asyncio.run(main())
```
{{/if}}

## Template Structure

- `{{templateFile}}` - Defines the sandbox template configuration
- `{{buildDevFile}}` - Builds the template for development
- `{{buildProdFile}}` - Builds the template for production

